            "text": "{\"description\":\"The first photograph shows a tall carved stone figure with a head-like upper portion, a broad torso, and shallow incised details. On the front are two small recessed oval features, a central raised circular ring, curving parallel bands below it, and several faint linear or animal-like incisions on the chest and neck area. The surface is worn and uneven, making many lines hard to distinguish.\",\"avian\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"Some faint incised shapes near the upper chest could be read as animal-like, but no clear bird head or beak is reliably visible on the carved surface in the first photograph.\",\"box\":null},\"large_face\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"The overall upper stone form may suggest a head, but clear facial features forming a large human face are not visible enough on the main front surface.\",\"box\":null},\"scorpion\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"There are curving and segmented-looking incisions around the central chest area, but legs and an upturned segmented tail are not clear enough to identify a scorpion.\",\"box\":null},\"round_motif\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"A distinct circular raised ring or round motif is visible near the center of the torso, separate from the small recessed ovals above.\",\"box\":[0.385,0.505,0.56,0.59]},\"three_arches\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"Although there are broad curved parallel bands below the central circle, there are not three repeated arch-topped forms arranged side by side in a row.\",\"box\":null},\"limitations\":\"The stone surface is heavily worn and pitted, with shallow low-contrast carving and uneven lighting; background objects overlap visually near the right edge but were ignored.\"}",
